fact WorkItem(id: "WI-293", description: some(value: "Typer: consume declared variance facts (Covariant/Contravariant) in types_compatible / parameterized_compatible / join_types, instead of hardcoded uniform covariance. PROBLEM: variance is declared AS FACTS (proposal 035; stdlib/anthill/reflect/typing.anthill:117-151 — entity Covariant(sort: Symbol, param: Symbol) / Contravariant(sort, param), with no-fact=invariant / both=bivariant, plus indirection rules effective_covariant / effective_contravariant and a check_variance(?S,?P,?V1,?V2) resolver rule), but NOTHING consumes them: grep finds zero Rust readers of check_variance/Covariant/effective_*, and no stdlib rule queries check_variance either — the facts/rules are inert. Instead the typer hardcodes variance: parameterized_compatible (rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/typing.rs) checks every binding value covariantly via types_compatible(actual_val, expected_val) REGARDLESS of declared variance, so a contravariant or invariant parameter is checked covariantly (potential unsoundness — e.g. a function-typed or mutable-cell parameter); arrow_compatible separately hardcodes structural arrow variance (contravariant param, covariant result/effects). TASK: wire effective_covariant/effective_contravariant (or check_variance) into types_compatible/parameterized_compatible so per-parameter variance is honored: invariant default => exact/equal binding value; covariant => actual_val <: expected_val (current behavior); contravariant => expected_val <: actual_val (flipped); bivariant => either. Then extend WI-287's join_types to recurse into bindings using the same variance, so a covariant T gives join(Option[T=Cat], Option[T=Dog]) = Option[T=Animal] instead of the current conservative clash (today join_types can't form parameterized lubs — it only does sort_ref widening — so WI-287 deliberately left the synthesized result a sound common supertype, not the strict lub; this WI is what would make it a real lub for parameterized sorts). SCOPE: distinct from WI-184 (the variance INFERENCE algorithm, Open) — this CONSUMES hand-declared facts and can land before inference exists; it is the prerequisite that makes WI-184's output meaningful. OPTIONAL (proposal 035 line 178): fold the hardcoded arrow_compatible into Function[A,B] with covariant(Function,B)/contravariant(Function,A) facts for uniformity. TESTS: contravariant param rejected where covariant-checking would wrongly accept; invariant param requires exact binding; covariant join Option[Cat]/Option[Dog] => Option[Animal]; bivariant accepts either. Note: scaland has no typer (see WI-287), so rust-only."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-14T17:01:25Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-293", author: "user", content: "Sequencing vs the type-parameter-threading work (docs/design/expansion-during-unification.md §8): variance is a PARALLEL soundness track, OFF the critical path — the minimal threading example length(collect(List.iterator(xs))) is all-equality, no subtyping. Land AFTER WI-379 (bidirectional inference): variance lives in the types_compatible/parameterized_compatible primitive that WI-379's check step already calls, so route arg-vs-param AND result-vs-expected through that shared primitive (the 'one relation, several implementations that agree' invariant) — don't hand-roll a bypassing equality. SYNERGY: WI-379's args-before-expected ordering pins the operation type params by EQUALITY from arguments, so variance-aware SUBTYPING only applies to ground result-vs-expected/arg-vs-param checks, never to solving a metavariable through a <: constraint (the classic local-type-inference hazard); expected-first seeding would hit it, args-first sidesteps it. Independent of WI-380/368/376/374/381. The default-flip (covariant->invariant) touches the SAME shared primitive WI-356 provider-admissibility + WI-379 use — migrate carefully (035 'Risk: existing tests'). Framework note: variance is the ORDER relation (subtyping/join/meet), sibling of unification (equality), already SLD-rules-over-facts — a second citizen of WI-382/WI-010 resolver-as-typechecker (per-sort ordering, not only per-sort unification).", at: "2026-06-04T13:19:03Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-293", author: "user", content: "SOUNDNESS PRIMITIVE DELIVERED 2026-06-04 (parallel track; join/lub DEFERRED to WI-382 per the reframe). parameterized_compatible_view (kb/typing.rs) now honors DECLARED per-(sort,param) variance instead of checking every binding covariantly: covariant->actual<:expected; contravariant->expected<:actual (flipped); invariant(default)->both directions/equal; bivariant->either. declared_variance(kb,sort,param) reads the Covariant/Contravariant facts via the per-functor rule index (rules_by_functor + fact_head_named_args + same_symbol) — the idiom every typer fact reader uses; NOT SLD (the effective_*/check_variance stdlib rules stay unconsumed scaffolding for WI-184). Keyed on the EXPECTED base (the supertype contract; cross-base reachable via refines). SEAM (per expansion-during-unification.md sec8): variance lives IN the shared primitive WI-379 plugs into, not a hand-rolled bypass; WI-379 routes arg-vs-param + result-vs-expected through it with args-first (keeps variance subtyping off metavariable-through-<: solving). DEFAULT-FLIP migration (the \"Risk: existing tests\" caution): (1) Function gets variance facts contravariant(A)/covariant(B)/covariant(E) — REQUIRED for consistency with arrow_compatible/arrow_function_compatible, fixed the 2 WI-333 Function[E] row-subtyping regressions; (2) Iterable.Element + IndexedSeq.T get Covariant facts (element OUTPUT-only => covariant) to restore legitimate widening the flip broke; (3) PersistentCollection/MutableCollection/Cell/Set/Map STAY invariant (element in INPUT position e.g. insert(elem:Element) — covariant was UNSOUND; the flip correctly rejects it — this is the soundness win, not a regression). 4 regression tests (contravariant Function[A]; invariant Cell rejects widening; covariant Option preserved; read-only Iterable covariant vs PersistentCollection invariant). 1455 green (full workspace). /code-review: 1 thorough finder; FIXED bivariant/invariant arm subst-pollution (probe-clone + commit-on-success, mirroring join_types/WI-335 per-direction hygiene) + the Iterable/IndexedSeq covariance regression; latent footguns NOTED as unreachable (entity-Covariant-decl skip relies on no sort named Symbol; value-fact-head skip; legacy non-canonical List[Type] E binding bypasses canonical_effects_row). DEFERRED to WI-382 (recorded there): the variance-aware join_types PARAMETERIZED-LUB (Option[Cat]/Option[Dog]=>Option[Animal]) — needs construct + a meet, the order-relation half.", at: "2026-06-04T14:08:14Z")
